---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { products, shortName, hasPackImages, DATA_DATE_LABEL, CREATOR } from '../lib/products';
---

<Base title="About this prototype — Clean Cut Meals (student concept)" description="Sources, dates and limits of this student prototype.">
  <div class="wrap about">
    <h1 class="title">About this prototype</h1>
    <p>
      This is a student concept made for the MTU Brand Challenge 2026. It isn't an official Clean Cut Meals, Musgrave or SuperValu
      service, and nothing can be ordered here. No account, cookies or tracking are used.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the information comes from</h2>
    <p>
      Names, descriptions, ingredients, allergens, nutrition and storage are copied from each meal's SuperValu product page,
      data as of {DATA_DATE_LABEL}. Cooking instructions aren't on those pages, so this prototype asks you to follow the
      instructions on your pack.
    </p>
    <ul>
      {
        products.map((p) => (
          <li>
            <a href={p.card_url} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
              {shortName(p)} on SuperValu online<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>

    <h2>Images and design</h2>
    {
      hasPackImages ? (
        <p>
          Pack images are from the SuperValu product pages, with only the empty white background cropped. The bowl printed on
          each pack is a serving suggestion. SuperValu, Uber Eats and Just Eat logos belong to their owners and only mark
          where each link goes. Colours follow the Clean Cut Meals Brand Book (June 2026).
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p>
          This public version has no pack photos and no logo, because we haven't confirmed permission to publish them. Look
          for the pack in the chilled aisle; the colour band on each page matches the band on its pack. Colours follow the
          Clean Cut Meals Brand Book (June 2026).
        </p>
      )
    }
    <p>The brand typeface Rink isn't available to us, so Lexend (SIL Open Font License) stands in for it.</p>

    <h2>Creator &amp; enquiries</h2>
    <p>
      This solution was conceived by Ruslan Ovcharenko through research into existing market offerings. For enquiries about
      collaboration, adaptation or use of his original materials, please contact him.
    </p>
    <ul class="contacts">
      <li><a href={`mailto:${CREATOR.email}`}>{CREATOR.email}</a></li>
      <li><a href={`tel:${CREATOR.phoneHref}`}>{CREATOR.phone}</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about {
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .title {
    margin: var(--s2) 0 var(--s3);
    font-size: var(--fs-h2);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }
  h2 {
    margin: var(--s5) 0 var(--s2);
    font-size: var(--fs-h3);
  }
  p,
  li {
    margin: 0 0 var(--s3);
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 1.2em;
  }
  .contacts {
    padding-left: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .contacts a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 44px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
